# Worked example run config: namespace scaling at customer scale on ROSA (README,
# "Namespace scaling"): the core series. One in-place growth series of config-only
# namespaces with 1 Service each, grown 250 -> 1000 -> 2000 -> 4000 on ONE member, with
# a probe window per scoping (namespace, wide) at every step, then 2000 namespaces
# outside the mesh (unlabeled, then labeled). For the fixed-per-namespace vs
# per-service split, run a second sweep with CONTROLPLANE_SERVICES_PER_NAMESPACES=4,
# CONTROLPLANE_NAMESPACE_COUNTS=250,1000,2000 and CONTROLPLANE_OUTSIDE_MODES=none.
#
# Keys are config/options.env knobs (and SETUP_CONTEXTS); a flag still beats a key.
# Parsed, never sourced: KEY=value only, no $ or ` outside single quotes. This file
# drives the sweep (003), which passes the growth flags to 001, 002 and 005 itself.
#
# Needs istiod sized for about 6000 namespaces (8Gi was planned for the window; at the
# lab's 3Gi the memory guard stops the series early and records SKIPPED_MEM_GUARD).
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-rosa.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx> --dry-run
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-rosa.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx>
#   ./tests/controlplane/004-report-results.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-rosa.env \
#     --results-dir tests/controlplane/results/ns-scaling-rosa/sweep-<RUN_ID> --format markdown
# The report's REQUIRED pods-vs-config-only row needs the fresh calibration pair that
# configs/ns-scaling-lab.env shows (same commands with this config), reported from the
# results base dir. Run it before the series, while no namespace delete is queued, and
# from the same commit: the base-dir report warns when the sweeps it reads differ in
# Istio version or harness commit (it lists them as istio_versions and harness_shas).
# It fits each sweep's series on its own (labelled run=<RUN_ID>).
# The series ends undiscovered and the namespaces stay: deleting thousands of
# namespaces takes hours on OpenShift, so do not queue it inside the window (destroying
# the cluster removes them). Copy the sweep dir off the host before teardown.
#
# SETUP_CONTEXTS must list every mesh member (the memory guard samples istiod and the
# gateways on all of them). Keep real context names out of git: copy this file to
# tests/controlplane/configs/<name>.local.env (gitignored) and set them there:
# SETUP_CONTEXTS=<mesh-a-ctx>,<mesh-b-ctx>,<mesh-c-ctx>

# Growth series (003). none is close to namespace at this size (both keep each proxy to
# its own namespace), so the core run probes namespace and wide only.
CONTROLPLANE_MESH_SIZES=1
CONTROLPLANE_SERVICES_PER_NAMESPACES=1
CONTROLPLANE_NAMESPACE_COUNTS=250,1000,2000,4000
CONTROLPLANE_SIDECAR_SCOPINGS=namespace,wide
CONTROLPLANE_WORKLOAD_MODE=config-only
# 8 measurement pods; 8,32 adds the M-sweep at N=4000 (two more probe windows).
CONTROLPLANE_MEASUREMENT_POD_COUNTS=8
CONTROLPLANE_OUTSIDE_NAMESPACES=2000
CONTROLPLANE_OUTSIDE_MODES=unlabeled,labeled

# Windows and collection. Wide config dumps reach tens of MB at 4000 namespaces.
CONTROLPLANE_SETTLE_SEC=45
CONTROLPLANE_PROBE_SETTLE_SEC=45
CONTROLPLANE_CONFIG_DUMP_SAMPLES=4
CONTROLPLANE_CONFIG_DUMP_TIMEOUT_S=120
# 001's readiness wait and its Sidecar delete (a switch to none) at thousands of objects.
CONTROLPLANE_WAIT_TIMEOUT_SEC=900

# Safety and the end of the series (undiscover: no namespace deletes in the window).
CONTROLPLANE_MEM_STOP_PCT=70
CONTROLPLANE_SERIES_RETIRE=undiscover
# The plan's later-deletion estimate; set it to the rate the lab measured.
CONTROLPLANE_NS_DELETE_SEC_PER_NS=1.0

# Results under the repo root (gitignored); a sweep adds sweep-<RUN_ID>/.
CONTROLPLANE_RESULTS_DIR=tests/controlplane/results/ns-scaling-rosa
